          "collection_date": "2023-06-01",
          "description": {
            "comment": "Preble's meadow jumping mouse (Zapus hudsonius preblei) is a subspecies of meadow jumping mouse, endemic to the upland habitats of Colorado and Wyoming in North America. It is found nowhere else in the world. It is listed as Threatened under the United States Endangered Species Act (from Wikipedia entry). This cell sample was cultured from a 3mm ear clipping procured from a male individual procured by Robert Schorr of the US Fish and Wildlife Service and sourced by the Colorado Natural Heritage Program. The sample was coordinated by Ben Novak of Revive & Restore and cultured by Sanaz Arenivas of ViaGen Pets to generate a high-quality reference genome for the Vertebrate Genomes Project (VGP). Sequencing and genome assembly were conducted at the Vertebrate Genome Lab (VGL) at the Rockefeller University, led by Erich D. Jarvis, Giulio Formenti, and Jennifer Balacco.",
